Use optional chaining and null/undefined guards when mapping over `nodes`, `edges`, `postures`, and `sources` in `validateKgV1RuntimeSpine` to ensure the validator fails closed gracefully instead of throwing unhandled exceptions on malformed entries.

```suggestion
  const duplicateNodeIds = duplicateValues(nodes.map((node) => node?.node_id));
  const duplicateEdgeIds = duplicateValues(edges.map((edge) => edge?.edge_id));
  const duplicatePostureIds = duplicateValues(postures.map((posture) => posture?.posture_id));
  const duplicateSourceIds = duplicateValues(sources.map((source) => source?.source_id));
  const nodeIds = new Set(nodes.map((node) => node?.node_id).filter(Boolean));
  const missingEndpointEdgeIds = edges
    .filter((edge) => edge && (!nodeIds.has(edge.from_node_id) || !nodeIds.has(edge.to_node_id)))
    .map((edge) => edge?.edge_id)
    .sort(compareByteOrder);
